cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use agt in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "agt: a local framework for multi-agent teams"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: blacsheep
repository-code: "https://github.com/blacsheep/agt"
license: MIT
version: 0.5.0
keywords:
  - multi-agent
  - llm
  - agents
  - mcp
  - codex
abstract: >-
  agt runs a team of AI agents on a local machine. It manages agent resources
  (providers, models, prompts, skills, MCP servers and harnesses), provides a
  shared IM with direct and group chats, and drives agents with a persistent
  scheduler so they can collaborate, delegate tasks and report back. A lead
  agent can create teammates, have Codex build MCP tools and attach them to
  the agents that need them.
